{#
  The hero at the top of a service-style page, once.

  It was written out four times — commercial-painter-cairns.njk,
  industrial-painting.njk, roof-painter-cairns.njk and services.njk — the same
  eleven lines each, varying only in the words and the two buttons.

  ⚠️ WORDS ARE DATA, LINKS ARE STRUCTURE. The eyebrow, the heading and the lede come
  from the page's content row, because those are the things a business actually wants
  to change. The buttons do not: their targets are navigation, one of them is an
  in-page anchor and another is built from site.phone_link, and none of that belongs in
  a content row. They are passed in as a block instead, so each page keeps its own
  pair without this file knowing anything about them.

  ⚠️ THE HEADING GOES THROUGH `heading`, WHICH IS WHY IT CAN BE STORED AT ALL. These
  h1s carry a line break and a highlighted phrase. See the filter in eleventy.config.js
  — a stored heading is text, a line break becomes a break, and a phrase in double
  square brackets becomes the highlight. Escaping happens first, so no stored value can
  produce any other tag. `safe` here is applied to output the filter has already
  escaped; it is not a shortcut past escaping.

  ⚠️ EACH PIECE IS GUARDED SEPARATELY. A missing lede must leave no empty paragraph
  behind, which is the defect this page had before.

  Usage — note the block form, which supplies the buttons:
    {% from "page-hero.njk" import pageHero %}
    {% call pageHero(svc.hero_eyebrow, svc.h1, svc.intro) %}
      <a class="btn btn--yellow btn--lg" href="/contact-us/">Get a quote</a>
    {% endcall %}
#}
{% macro pageHero(eyebrow, h1, lede) -%}
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    {%- if eyebrow %}
    <span class="eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</span>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if h1 %}
    <h1 style="margin-top:14px">{{ h1 | heading | safe }}</h1>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if lede %}
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px;max-width:62ch">
      {{ lede }}
    </p>
    {%- endif %}
    <div style="margin-top:28px;display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap">
      {{- caller() }}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endmacro %}
